    "body": "Fair enough. I think what people are asking for is some level of standardisation of some of those layers. Otherwise as a maintainer of a shared implementation, we can't really introduce bespoke layering without being opinionated (and as you said, not following a standard).\r\n\r\nIs there any case where browsers actually do need to specify null values? e.g. `<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"x\">` followed by `x.value = null`?",
